Spring Framework ek Java framework hai jo Java applications ko develop karna easy banata hai.
Ye mainly IOC (Inversion of Control) aur Dependency Injection (DI) provide karta hai, jisse objects ko manually create aur manage karne ki zarurat nahi padti.
"Spring Framework ek lightweight Java framework hai jo Dependency Injection aur IOC ke through loosely coupled applications banane me help karta hai."
Spring me object hum nahi banate. 
Bean:-Jo object Spring banata aur manage karta hai, usko Bean kehte hain.

IOC(Inversion of Control): IOC Container Spring ka manager hai. 
Ye:
* Objects (Beans) create karta hai
* Dependencies inject karta hai. Dependency Injection ke liye IOC Container ko metadata dena padta hai, jo XML configuration ya annotations (@Component, @Autowired) ke through provide kiya ja sakta hai.
* Beans ko manage karta hai

Metadata kya hota hai?
IOC Container ko batana padta hai ki:   
* Kaunsi classes Bean hain?
* Kaunsi dependency inject karni hai?

Ye information hi Metadata kehlati hai.

Metadata dene ke 2 tareeke hain:
1. XML
2. Annotations

IOC container ka naam hai "ApplicationContext". ApplicationContext Spring IOC Container ka advanced implementation hai jo beans ko create, configure aur manage karta hai.
ApplicationContext context = new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext("beans.xml");



